Subject: [PATCH] Runtime: the game's vibration on Xbox (XInput) controllers (TODO 200)

A gamepad read through GLFW had no rumble; only the native DualSense / DualShock 4 path (0008) vibrated. On
Windows ps2_xinput_rumble writes the motors of the first connected XInput pad while a GLFW gamepad drives the PS2
pad, from the same guest actuator data the Sony path uses (small on/off -> wRightMotorSpeed, large 0..255 ->
wLeftMotorSpeed, scaled by PS2X_SONYPAD_RUMBLE). Ticked on the window thread, so the motors stop when the window
loses focus, while the game's input is blocked, when the game stops reading the pad for 300 ms (paused,
loading) and at exit; a state load clears the guest motors (Sony pads too). XInput1_4.dll, else XInput9_1_0.dll,
loaded at run time on the first vibration: no new link dependency. Never in a hidden window.
PS2X_XINPUT_TRACE=1 logs the motor changes; =2 also calls in a hidden window without a pad (test machines).

